{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"doubly_linked","title":"Doubly Linked List","group":"","order":13,"html":"<p>None &lt;--&gt; 10 &lt;--&gt; 20 &lt;--&gt; 30 &lt;--&gt; None</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n  def __init__(self, data):\n    self.data = data\n    self.prev = None\n    self.next = None\n\nhead = Node(10)\ntemp1 = Node(20)\ntemp2 = Node(30)\n\nhead.next = temp1\ntemp1.prev = head\n\ntemp1.next = temp2\ntemp2.prev = temp1\n\ntemp = head\nwhile temp is not None:\n  print(temp.data)\n  temp = temp.next</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Advantages</h3>\n<p>1. can be traversed in both directions</p>\n<p>2. A given delete a node in O(1) time with given reference/pointer to it</p>\n<p>3. Insert/Delete before a given node</p>\n<p>4. Insert/Delete from both ends in O(1) time by maintaining tail</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Disadvantages</h3>\n<p>1. Extra Space for prev</p>\n<p>2. Code becomes more complex</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Insert at beginning</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Insert at beginning\n\nclass Node:\n  def __init__(self, data):\n    self.data = data\n    self.prev = None\n    self.next = None\n\ndef printList(head):\n    temp = head\n    while temp is not None:\n      print(temp.data, end = ' ')\n      temp = temp.next\n\ndef insertAtBeginning(head, data):\n    temp = Node(data)\n    temp.next = head\n    head.prev = temp\n    return temp\n\nhead = Node(10)\ntemp1 = Node(20)\ntemp2 = Node(30)\n\nhead.next = temp1\ntemp1.prev = head\n\ntemp1.next = temp2\ntemp2.prev = temp1\n\nhead = insertAtBeginning(head, 5)\n\nprintList(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Insert at the End</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def insertEnd(head, x):\n  temp = Node(x)\n  if head == None:\n    return temp\n\n  curr = head\n  while curr.next is not None:\n    curr = curr.next\n\n  curr.next = temp\n  temp.prev = curr\n\n  return head\n\nhead = insertEnd(head, 40)\nprintList(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Delete head</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def delHead(head):\n  if head == None:\n    return None\n\n  if head.next == None:\n    return None\n\n  head = head.next\n  head.prev = None\n  return head\n\nhead = delHead(head)\nprintList(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Delete last Node</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def delEnd(head):\n  if head == None:\n    return None\n\n  if head.next == None:\n    return None\n\n  curr = head\n  while curr.next.next is not None:\n    curr = curr.next\n\n  curr.next = None\n  return head\n\nhead = delEnd(head)\nprintList(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Reverse a Double Linked List</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def reverseDLL(head):\n  if head == None:\n    return None\n\n  if head.next == None:\n    return head\n\n  curr = head\n  prev = None\n\n  while curr != None:\n    prev = curr\n    curr.next, curr.prev = curr.prev, curr.next\n    curr = curr.prev\n\n  return prev\n\nhead = reverseDLL(head)\nprintList(head)</code></pre></figure></section>"}